From: Valerie Snyder <valsnyde@cisco.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:23:19 -0400
Subject: libclamav: Validate yC buffer offsets (#154)

A modified-yC PE can supply a raw section offset smaller than the
negative adjustment used by the unpacker. The resulting unsigned wrap
forms pointers outside the copied file buffer, while the existing
bounds helper narrows the pointer difference and can accept the access.

Calculate and validate yC offsets as integers before forming addresses,
and keep emulator accesses as checked buffer-relative offsets. This
prevents malformed files from terminating the scanner.

Reported by Nebula Security.

CLAM-3068

---
Upstream: https://github.com/Cisco-Talos/clamav/commit/4993d6787d82cb55928fccc1cc88150f02478a37
CVE: CVE-2026-76415
